#If you want to check that your code is doing the right thing and it aligns with your logics that "what will be the output".

#There are two types of test:-

#Console Output Test -> In this testing mechanism there is noting fancy, you just check the functioning of the code with the output you got and it matches with your assumptions. It is good for small projects but as the data grows and complexity arises this method initially fails.
#Unit Test -> Now this is the industrial standard. In this the project splits like for the main it is (main.py) and for a testing scripts (main_test.py) and it is mostly hidden, and you can leave the print function as it is (it only checks the return statement's output).

#Debugging -> It means correcting the code untils it doesn't matches the developer's need and the output or functionality the developer expects.